// == E-graph refresher: computing congruence closure

// To insert a term: flatten it leaf-to-root, looking up or inserting an equivalence class
// for each E-node

// == E-graph refresher: computing congruence closure

// To merge terms: call union() on the union-find

// == E-graph refresher: computing congruence closure

// To compute the congruence closure, we have to do rebuild()

// #pause

// 1. For every E-node $f(e_1, e_2, ...)$, update it to $f("find"(e_1), "find"(e_2))$

// #pause

// 2. Whenever we have $f(e_1, e_2, ...) in e_j$ and also $in e_k$, call union($e_j, e_k$)

// #pause

// A bit slow (maybe). But we can defer rebuilding and/or use Downey-Sethi-Tarjan (aka binarizing the function symbols)

